This integration was written by an AI model (Anthropic Claude Opus 5).

The local REST API of Samsung washing machines on port 8888 was mapped out for this
project by probing the appliance directly. The starting point was the observation that
the appliance's own TLS handshake advertises which client CAs it accepts, and that one
of them - AC14K_M - is publicly mirrored together with its private key:
  https://github.com/brayStorm/samsung-appliance-token

Prior work consulted while building this:
  https://github.com/hmmferreira/samsung-aircon-8888-get-token  (the token callback flow)
  https://github.com/atxbyea/samsungrac                         (port 8888, air conditioners)
  https://github.com/QuiteYellow/SmartThings-Local              (the AC14K_M chain, CoAP-DTLS generation)
  https://github.com/mbillow/localthings                        (CoAP-DTLS generation)

The wash programme code map in const.py is specific to a TP6X_WW6500 (EU, 14-position
dial) and was calibrated empirically. Other models will report different codes; unknown
codes are surfaced as "unknown" with the raw value kept in an attribute.
